1
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:17,520
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa River,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
I kick a pebble and my shoe flies off too.

3
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:32,920
Right onto the head of the
carpenter who'd been saving up,

4
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:39,120
I got laughed at for
still acting like a kid.

5
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I chase after some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:46,100
Pachinko Kameari.

7
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:49,280
A single yawn changes nothing.

8
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,180
The town's streets feel strangely gentle.

9
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,140
From the pointed hat's water basin,

10
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:07,440
the sun sinks toward the great observatory.

11
00:01:11,220 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow, too,
it'll end just like this, won't it?

12
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,060
Katsushika Shibamata,
again, losing even happiness.

13
00:01:27,580 --> 00:01:31,540
The Great Newspaper War.

14
00:01:54,420 --> 00:01:55,540
No bicycle.

15
00:01:55,540 --> 00:01:57,100
In other words,

16
00:01:58,080 --> 00:01:58,900
Lucky!

17
00:01:58,900 --> 00:02:01,160
If Ryo-san shows up,
that means he's out on patrol, right?

18
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:03,200
Nao-chan, I'm so happy!

19
00:02:03,580 --> 00:02:06,080
Let's get this done quickly
while the idiot's away.

20
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:09,260
Hiya!

21
00:02:09,260 --> 00:02:12,200
It's the Katsushika Police Station newsletter,
"Green Light."

22
00:02:12,660 --> 00:02:14,380
You're here early.

23
00:02:14,380 --> 00:02:17,680
Isn't "Green Light" the one
posted in the station hallways?

24
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:18,920
That's right.

25
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:22,940
We also deliver on request.

26
00:02:22,940 --> 00:02:26,620
It's a paper that's hugely popular with
the policewomen of Katsushika Station.

27
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:28,940
I've seen this one before.

28
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:30,020
So, today's

29
00:02:30,580 --> 00:02:33,020
is a feature on Reiko Akimoto.

30
00:02:33,920 --> 00:02:36,880
We're going to reveal Reiko's
private clothes in the paper!

31
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:37,960
Reiko-san, please.

32
00:02:38,780 --> 00:02:39,600
Got it.

33
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:42,120
I'll go change in the back,
so wait here a moment.

34
00:02:58,480 --> 00:03:00,360
This is really bad, senpai.

35
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:01,680
Idiot, don't make a sound.

36
00:03:04,760 --> 00:03:06,960
I wonder when someone put up this poster.

37
00:03:08,340 --> 00:03:10,240
This poster looks strangely out of place.

38
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:14,140
Is it just my imagination?

39
00:03:15,940 --> 00:03:16,260
Okay.

40
00:03:16,980 --> 00:03:18,600
This is bad, s-senpai.

41
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:23,720
Ryo-chan!

42
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:26,920
Hey, Reiko.
What are you doing in a place like this?

43
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:31,700
Peeping at a woman's changing room?
That's despicable!

44
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:35,511
But don't say that! I just happened
to be inside with Honda when,

45
00:03:35,561 --> 00:03:38,520
you came in and started
taking your clothes off!

46
00:03:38,860 --> 00:03:40,180
Lame excuse...

47
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:40,780
What did you say?

48
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:42,460
Reiko-san, is something wrong?

49
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:44,920
I heard a strange noise,
so I'm opening the door!

50
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:45,600
Go ahead!

51
00:03:48,340 --> 00:03:49,620
Ryo Kankichi!

52
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:51,280
Hey!

53
00:03:51,700 --> 00:03:52,780
What's going on?

54
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,420
He's a peeping Tom!

55
00:03:54,780 --> 00:03:55,480
What?!

56
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:57,480
I told you, it's not what it looks like!

57
00:03:58,440 --> 00:04:01,260
So that's why you kept pushing so hard
to find out when the interview was!

58
00:04:01,260 --> 00:04:03,160
You enemy of women, you pervert!

59
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:05,300
It's a misunderstanding,
I swear it's a misunderstanding!

60
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:07,420
Then what's that camera for?

61
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:10,080
Well, this is just a coincidence...

62
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:11,200
What is this?

63
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:11,860
That's...

64
00:04:11,860 --> 00:04:14,220
"Dokkiri Sexy Photo, Confiscate Them All"?

65
00:04:14,380 --> 00:04:16,220
First prize: 200,000 yen!

66
00:04:16,220 --> 00:04:18,320
So this is what you were after!

67
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:21,220
If we get the shots,
we split the prize, right?

68
00:04:21,220 --> 00:04:22,540
Hey, help me out here.

69
00:04:23,960 --> 00:04:26,120
As if I would!

70
00:04:29,460 --> 00:04:39,480


71
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:45,180
This is the boss's fault, but surely

72
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:46,900
you'll make sure to...

73
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:48,140
I can't believe it.

74
00:04:50,780 --> 00:04:54,360
Whoa! You went sniffing around
and made up all sorts of stuff!

75
00:04:55,340 --> 00:04:58,620
But you did peep, so it can't be helped.

76
00:04:59,020 --> 00:05:01,980
It was only an attempt! You left out the part about just looking around,
didn't you?

77
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:05,560
If this has taught you a lesson, you'd
better keep your head down from now on.

78
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:06,180
Exactly, exactly.

79
00:05:07,380 --> 00:05:10,780
Honestly, I'd be relieved if you just
vanished from the police force, but

80
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:28,640
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu

81
00:05:28,640 --> 00:05:30,340
So that's how it was?

82
00:05:30,860 --> 00:05:34,600
Ryotsu 13:
Trends in the year-end party dojo-sukui act

83
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:37,131
If you run out of material
and have no other choice,

84
00:05:37,181 --> 00:05:38,640
I'll give you a little bit of coverage.

85
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:39,640
R-really?

86
00:05:39,700 --> 00:05:40,540
Say cheese!

87
00:05:43,020 --> 00:05:44,100
Leave it to me.

88
00:05:44,860 --> 00:05:45,840
Here, the preparations...

89
00:05:45,840 --> 00:05:49,780
You idiots, all of you!

90
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:50,860
What's his deal!

91
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:55,540
That damn brat!

92
00:05:56,740 --> 00:06:00,300
Why do I have to practice
the Dojo Sukui dance?

93
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:03,260
But they looked like they
were having a pretty good time.

94
00:06:03,260 --> 00:06:06,520
I'll never forgive them.
I'm getting my revenge!

95
00:06:06,520 --> 00:06:10,220
But if we make a careless move,
won't it end up in the newspaper again?

96
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:12,480
I have a good idea.

97
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:16,960
I'll make them taste every bit
of the humiliation I suffered.

98
00:06:21,180 --> 00:06:23,160
Just you wait, you idiots.

99
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:26,840
But they'll pay in full
for angering Kankichi Ryotsu!

100
00:06:27,300 --> 00:06:29,220
I've got so many good ideas...

101
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:42,480
Anyone tougher than Ken?

102
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:44,920
Ryo-san, long time no see.

103
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:47,220
Still as unmotivated at work as ever

104
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:49,180
Reading a sports paper on duty?

105
00:06:49,180 --> 00:06:50,580
That's no different from me, is it?

106
00:06:50,580 --> 00:06:53,060
Don't you need to check your own paper?

107
00:06:53,060 --> 00:06:57,300
It's fine. Nobody reads our paper anyway.

108
00:06:57,680 --> 00:06:58,300
This is

109
00:06:58,300 --> 00:07:02,380
the editorial office of the Katsushika Police Station's official newsletter,
the Katsushika Shimbun.

110
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:05,320
And this is the editor-in-chief,
Ken, stronger than anyone.

111
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:05,940
Hello.

112
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:09,900
I thought the newsletter was just the
"Green Light," wasn't it?

113
00:07:09,900 --> 00:07:12,120
I've never actually seen any others, though.

114
00:07:12,120 --> 00:07:14,180
It's pasted up in the corner
of the hallway, though.

115
00:07:14,180 --> 00:07:16,460
It's so dull that nobody looks at it.

116
00:07:16,460 --> 00:07:19,160
Especially with the
editor-in-chief in this state.

117
00:07:20,580 --> 00:07:20,900
I'm telling you.

118
00:07:22,100 --> 00:07:24,280
Actually, I have a favor to ask you.

119
00:07:25,200 --> 00:07:26,100
W-what is it?

120
00:07:26,100 --> 00:07:29,360
Hand over this editor-in-chief seat to me.

121
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:32,600
D-d-don't say such crazy things!

122
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:34,860
I refuse, I'm telling you.

123
00:07:35,260 --> 00:07:37,975
Didn't you, just the other day,
nail the Kikuka Sho prediction,

124
00:07:38,025 --> 00:07:40,100
hit the jackpot big-time,

125
00:07:40,100 --> 00:07:42,100
and let me make a fortune?

126
00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:46,220
Who was it that got you
to bet with all you had?

127
00:07:46,220 --> 00:07:49,300
Th-that was all thanks to you, Ryo-san.

128
00:07:50,580 --> 00:07:51,236
Yeah, but you...

129
00:07:51,286 --> 00:07:54,680
Didn't you grovel and swear to your
wife you'd never gamble on horses again?

130
00:07:54,680 --> 00:08:00,000
If she finds out you're
still buying betting tickets...

131
00:08:00,820 --> 00:08:02,100
Please get out!

132
00:08:10,300 --> 00:08:11,500
Fine, fine.

133
00:08:11,500 --> 00:08:13,620
Good, as long as you understand.

134
00:08:13,620 --> 00:08:15,500
But only for a little while, got it?

135
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:16,980
I know, I know.

136
00:08:17,980 --> 00:08:19,440
Heh-heh-heh-heh!

137
00:08:19,440 --> 00:08:22,500
What exactly do you plan to do once
you're editor-in-chief of a newspaper?

138
00:08:22,740 --> 00:08:24,060
Hammurabi Hoten!

139
00:08:24,840 --> 00:08:28,660
An eye for an eye, a tooth for a tooth,
and a newspaper for a newspaper, wasa!

140
00:08:28,660 --> 00:08:32,580
We'll expose the corruption of Komachi
and Naoko and blast it all over our paper.

141
00:08:32,580 --> 00:08:34,000
Taishihei!

142
00:08:34,980 --> 00:08:36,580
Keiokiru!

143
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:38,420
Phew.

144
00:08:38,420 --> 00:08:38,940
Eeeh!

145
00:08:38,940 --> 00:08:40,260
Hahahaha!

146
00:08:47,700 --> 00:08:48,560
W-why?

147
00:08:49,100 --> 00:08:51,660
We're finally out of the boss's sight,

148
00:08:51,660 --> 00:08:53,100
