234
00:12:19,160 --> 00:12:23,520
We don't need something that puts people
on display like those women's weeklies!

235
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:27,060
That's not true! It's the Katsushika
newsletter that isn't needed!

236
00:12:27,380 --> 00:12:28,000
That's right!

237
00:12:28,860 --> 00:12:31,065
Even if you say that,

238
00:12:31,115 --> 00:12:33,780
you two, what am I supposed to do...

239
00:12:38,560 --> 00:12:40,500
Fine, then let's settle this with a contest.

240
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:41,580
A contest?

241
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:45,740
We'll see which of us deserves to
be Katsushika's official newsletter.

242
00:12:45,740 --> 00:12:48,380
Sounds interesting. How will we decide?

243
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:53,240
Every time the latest issue of both papers comes out,
we'll hold a popularity vote using ballots,

244
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:58,080
and the paper with the higher popularity in the end
wins and becomes Katsushika's only official newsletter.

245
00:12:58,080 --> 00:13:00,600
Of course, the losing paper
gets discontinued immediately.

246
00:13:01,400 --> 00:13:05,060
I'll tell you now, what matters in a
newspaper is winning the readers' hearts.

247
00:13:05,060 --> 00:13:09,160
If you're not confident, then quit
that junk paper of yours right now.

248
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:12,500
Who said we're not confident? Bring it on.

249
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:15,260
We accept this contest. Let's do it!

250
00:13:16,680 --> 00:13:18,680
Don't blame me, don't blame me!

251
00:13:19,140 --> 00:13:22,960
Just watch,
I'm going to crush your rotten newspaper.

252
00:13:23,360 --> 00:13:27,000
That's my line!
You'd better be ready, you idiot.

253
00:13:45,460 --> 00:13:48,860
